## Practical habits that worked (game 2)
- Area scoring: dame points count, so fill neutral points (e.g. F4) at the end
  as long as my group keeps two real eyes.
- Before passing, capture any dead enemy stones inside my area outright.
- Quick count method: my stones + empty points I surround; add 7 komi when White.

## Tools
- after.py: `python3 after.py <MOVE> <X|O> <<'EOF' ...board rows... EOF` places the move,
  removes captures, and lists every group's libs after it. Use it on EVERY candidate move.
- libs.py (in workdir): paste the board() rows into stdin -> lists every group's
  liberties and flags groups with <=2 libs. RUN IT EVERY MOVE from move ~30 on, and
  check the board you would get after your planned move, not just the current one.
- Board coordinates: columns A-J skipping I; rows 1-9 bottom to top.
- Can use shell to count liberties / area (allowed: inspection only).
- Game 42: lost to 12k as White (engine judged my alive top group dead). As White
  vs 12k: 7-6-2. Next: if White, 12k again (opening C4 + G3 vs E5 F7 was OK);
  before passing, run libs.py and make sure every group has 2 split single-point eyes.
  If Black, 14k with C3/G3/E5.
